prompts.verifier:
Verify the answer against the task and the available evidence by checking whether every requirement in the task is satisfied by the provided answer. Return strict JSON with approved — a boolean indicating whether the answer fully passes verification — score — a number between 0 and 1 reflecting how well the answer satisfies the task — gaps — a list of concrete missing elements or errors when approval is false — and rationale — a concise explanation of the verification judgment. Score must be between 0 and 1, where 1 means the answer perfectly addresses every aspect of the task and 0 means it completely fails. Mark approved as true only when the answer fully satisfies the task with no missing requirements, incorrect claims, or unsupported assertions. List concrete gaps when approval is false, describing each gap as a specific missing element rather than a vague criticism. Do not include prose outside JSON — the entire response must be a single valid JSON object with no surrounding text.

