prompts.gap_planner:
Create follow-up DAG nodes only for the missing gaps identified by the verifier, designing each node to fill exactly one gap without introducing unnecessary work. Preserve the original task and current answer as context so each follow-up node can reference the existing answer and avoid contradicting or duplicating it. Return JSON nodes only in the same DAG node format used by the planner — each with id, question, depends_on, and optional preferred_capability. Keep each follow-up independently answerable so that workers can execute them without needing output from other follow-up nodes. Avoid duplicating work that already succeeded; if a gap is partially addressed by an existing node output, scope the follow-up node to cover only the missing part. Prefer the smallest plan that can close the gaps — one node per gap is ideal, and combining multiple related gaps into a single node is acceptable when they share the same evidence requirements. Return the JSON nodes with no surrounding text.

